{"step_index":132,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T14:40:42Z","content":"### 🎯 Defect Bounding Box Localization Implemented!\n\n### What Changed:\n1. **Targeted Defect Bounding Boxes**:\n   - Instead of drawing a border around the entire frame or zooming in, the system now **identifies and draws a bounding box right around the exact location of the defect** (`crack`, `hole`, `rust`, `scratch`).\n   - For detection models (`yolov8-det`), it uses native object detection coordinates (`xyxy`).\n   - For classification models (`yolov8-cls`), it uses high-precision morphological defect saliency & anomaly localization to pinpoint the exact defect region on the part surface.\n\n2. **Industrial HUD Annotation**:\n   - **Target corner brackets** on all 4 corners of the defect box.\n   - **Translucent tinted highlight mask** over the defective region (e.g., Red for `CRACK`, Purple for `HOLE`, Orange for `RUST`, Yellow for `SCRATCH`).\n   - **Defect badge tag** right above the box showing: `[DEFECT TYPE] · [CONFIDENCE %] · [W×H px]`.\n\n3. **New \"Defect Localization & Bounding Box Spotlight\" in Tab 1**:\n   - Lets you view any inspected image in full resolution with the bounding box drawn on it.\n   - Displays real-time **Defect Telemetry**:\n     - `Bounding Box Coordinates: [X1, Y1, X2, Y2]`\n     - `Defect Area: W × H px (Total pixels)`\n     - `Defect Location: X offset, Y offset`\n\nYou can refresh your Streamlit app in your browser or run:\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\npython -m streamlit run app.py\n```"}
