{"step_index":149,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T14:45:26Z","content":"### 🔧 Fixed!\n\n### Root Cause of the Error:\nIn OpenCV 5.0, `cv2.absdiff` rejected the NumPy scalar argument (`np.uint8(np.mean(a))`) because of strict overload type checking between NumPy scalar objects and OpenCV array buffers.\n\n### What Was Fixed:\nReplaced the operation in `modules/defect_detector.py` with vectorised NumPy float arithmetic:\n```python\na_f = a.astype(np.float32)\nb_f = b.astype(np.float32)\nab_var = np.abs(a_f - float(np.mean(a_f))) + np.abs(b_f - float(np.mean(b_f)))\n```\nAll defect localization routines (`crack`, `hole`, `rust`, `scratch`, `normal`) were tested and verified to execute without any errors.\n\nYou can now refresh your browser page or re-run the Streamlit application:\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\npython -m streamlit run app.py\n```"}
